  "aboutBody": "Muslimin helps Muslims find the jamat times of the masjids around them. Every masjid profile is created by its own authority and verified by our team before it becomes public.",
  "faqQ1": "Where do the jamat times come from?",
  "faqA1": "Each masjid's authority sets and updates its own jamat times. Prayer start times are calculated for your location.",
  "faqQ2": "Why is location mandatory?",
  "faqA2": "Location is used to show masjids near you and to calculate accurate prayer times. It is never shared with anyone.",
  "faqQ3": "How can I add my masjid?",
  "faqA3": "Go to More → Register a Masjid. You must be a committee member, imam, moazzin, khatib or khadem, and you must be inside the masjid while registering.",
  "faqQ4": "Why is my masjid not visible?",
  "faqA4": "New profiles are verified by our team before they become public. This usually takes 1–2 days.",
  "faqQ5": "How do jamat reminders work?",
  "faqA5": "Open a masjid and tap the bell on Jamat Time. You will be notified 15, 30 or 45 minutes before each jamat, even when the app is closed.",
